//! Generated protobuf types.
//!
//! All three schemas in `proto/` share the same `package touchy;`
//! declaration, so prost emits a single `touchy.rs` containing every
//! message and enum. We re-export it under [`crate::proto`] so
//! downstream code writes `use touchy_pad::proto::Screen;` instead of
//! reaching into generated module paths.
//!
//! The file is **checked in** (`src/proto/touchy.rs`) instead of being
//! generated by a build script, so building this crate needs neither
//! `protoc` nor `prost-build` — the same deal the Python package offers,
//! where the generated `_pb2` modules ship inside the wheel. Regenerate it
//! with `just rust-gen-proto` (or `just build-proto`, which also refreshes
//! the Python/C bindings) after editing `proto/*.proto`; CI fails if it is
//! stale. Never hand-edit it.
//!
//! Lints are muted for the generated items below, mirroring the Python side
//! (`pyproject.toml` `[tool.ruff] extend-exclude` skips the generated
//! `_pb2` modules): what prost emits is upstream-controlled. Only this module
//! is affected — it holds nothing but the `include!`.
#![allow(missing_docs)]
#![allow(clippy::all)]

include!(concat!(env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"), "/src/proto/touchy.rs"));
